| 820 |\n   741\t| — | stays | `tests/test_revision9_coordination.py` | `Revision9BuilderBatchTests` | 1 (skipUnless) | 0 | source ≈4,900 after the wave |\n   742\t\n   743\tMachine-readable copy of the families (order, csv, expected headers, helpers, sizes): `.refactor/families-revision9-coord.json`.\n   744\t\n   745\t# Reviewer context from the overnight brief 2026-09-23 (operator rulings and allowed deviations)\n   746\t\n   747\t## Brief section 4 item 1 (config-only prep, including the operator rulings of 11:30 and 14:10)\n   748\t1. **Config-only prep, before any move** (session-2 lesson): pyproject.toml\n   749\t   `[tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores]` gains two temporary globs, `\"tests/test_<stem>_*.py\"` and\n   750\t   `\"tests/_<name>_*.py\"`, whose list is the source file's current entry (pyproject lines 242,\n   751\t   244, 245) MINUS `I001`; plus provisional `.refactor-baseline.json` entries for every planned\n   752\t   module over 500 (added once the plan is approved, still before the first family cluster).\n   753\t   **Operator ruling 2026-09-23 11:30 on both lanes' stop finding (import bootstrap order):** the\n   754\t   same config-only prep, in a commit that precedes the mixin commit, adds\n   755\t\n   756\t   ```toml\n   757\t   [tool.ruff.lint.isort]\n   758\t   known-local-folder = [\"codex_orchestrator\", \"codex_orch_tools\", \"forge_cli\", \"commitment_paths\"]\n   759\t   ```\n   760\t\n   761\t   Measured on the whole repository (`ruff check --select I scripts tests system/fr223`): zero new\n   762\t   findings; a generated header then places `from tests._<name>_constants import ...` above the\n   763\t   `codex_orchestrator` / `codex_orch_tools` / `forge_cli` imports, so the constants module's\n   764\t   `sys.path` line runs first and every family module imports standalone without PYTHONPATH.\n   765\t   The driver keeps lane B's standalone-import check per module. That commit also removes the\n   766\t   lane's `STOPPED-<name>.md` (superseded by this ruling) and is the only place this ruling is\n   767\t   applied; the mixin dry run is re-run under it with the same argv before the apply.\n   768\t   **Operator ruling 2026-09-23 14:10 on both lanes' wave-close stop (legacy-name carve-out):**\n   769\t   `tests/test_migration.py` `LegacyRuntimeNameCarveOutTests` scans every tracked file for the\n   770\t   legacy runtime name, and the brief's `tests`-scoped ID and body snapshots under `.refactor/`\n   771\t   quote that test's own name and fixtures. Ruling: one config-class prep commit per lane adds\n   772\t   `\".refactor/\"` to that test's `allowed_prefixes` tuple (the evidence files are verbatim copies of\n   773\t   test source the test already allows for itself), removes the wave-close `STOPPED-<name>.md`,\n   774\t   and is followed by the wave-close Gate 1 re-run. This is the one permitted edit to a test\n   775\t   outside the target file. The separate question of the evidence directory shipping with plugin\n   776\t   installs is bead forge-plugin-xlt7 (see section 10), not a lane matter.\n   777\t   Without the glob the gate's `ruff check tests` fails on the first family module that\n   778\t   inherits a PLR0904/PLR0915 finding. Finalize replaces the globs with measured per-module\n   779\t   entries and deletes them.\n   780\t\n   781\t## Brief section 11 (verified tonight, and the three allowed deviations)\n   782\t## 11. Verified tonight, and the three allowed deviations\n   783\t\n   784\tLane A's first run stopped at its first commit because the worktree-local `\"forge@forge\": false`\n   785\tdid not disable the plugin; section 1 records the corrected layout. Both lanes' second runs\n   786\tstopped at 02:25 on the import bootstrap order of generated headers (their `STOPPED-*.md` and\n   787\tcritiques hold the shard simulations); section 4 item 1 records the operator's ruling.\n   788\tDry-run on a throwaway worktree of 69bc28d (removed afterwards; nothing committed anywhere):\n   789\tthe worktree plus settings file leaves git status empty; the focused discover commands collect\n   790\t81/85/144 tests; the ID and body snapshots take 5 s and 4 s; `verify.sh --pkg tests ... --fast`\n   791\tpasses every step with the section-1 env; the mixin move of all 31 lane-B1 helpers verifies\n   792\tclean once the constants module exists; the class-shape dry run before the mixin commit refuses\n   793\tas designed. Three plugin behaviours do not fit this repository's namespace `tests/` layout;\n   794\teach has a bounded workaround here and a follow-up in the plugin repo:\n   795\t\n   796\t1. **rope_move.py fails on the `Path(__file__)`-derived constants** (`ROOT`, `TOOLS`:\n   797\t   `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'group'` with `--project tests`; a silent\n   798\t   no-op with `--project .`). The constants module is therefore hand-written (section 4, item 2)\n   799\t   under the plan's \"layout-only preparation commit\" clause; it is disclosed to both reviewers\n   800\t   and in the handover as the session's one hand-written commit.\n   801\t2. **The mover replaces `--import-root .` with the collector's top (`tests`)** and would write\n   802\t   a bare `from _<name>_support import`, unimportable under the Gate 1 cell's\n   803\t   `python3 -m unittest tests.<module>`. Pass `--import-root \"$PWD\"` on every mixin and class\n   804\t   move; the import then reads `from tests._<name>_support import ...`, the form the file's\n   805\t   existing `from tests._cli_loader import ...` already uses.\n   806\t3. **verify.sh's type step cannot run mypy over `tests/`** (\"Source file found twice under\n   807\t   different module names\", exit 2, whatever MYPYPATH). `REFACTOR_TYPE_CMD` in the worktree\n   808\t   settings points it at `scripts/forge/forge_cli`, which these sessions must not change; the\n   809\t   check runs in 4 s against the tracked baseline (234 grandfathered, 0 new) and the production\n   810\t   diff check in section 4 covers the rest.\n   811\t\n   812\tA fourth finding shapes the recipe rather than deviating from it: the mixin cannot be moved into\n   813\tthe module that defines the constants its helpers read (`destination import name clash`), hence\n   814\tthe separate `_<name>_constants.py` and `_<name>_support.py`.\n   815\t\n    55\t\n    56\t    cached = sys.modules.get(name)\n    57\t    if cached is not None:\n    58\t        return cached\n    59\t    return load_script(name, path)\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\tdef package_module(name: str) -> ModuleType:\n    63\t    \"\"\"Import ``forge_cli.<name>`` once, exactly as the shim does, and return it.\n    64\t\n    65\t    The package modules are canonical (one object shared by every loaded CLI\n    66\t    instance), so a test that patches a moved control patches it here, not on a\n    67\t    per-module copy of the name.\n    68\t    \"\"\"\n    69\t\n    70\t    scripts_dir = str(SCRIPTS_DIR)\n    71\t    if scripts_dir not in sys.path:\n    72\t        sys.path.insert(0, scripts_dir)\n    73\t    return importlib.import_module(f\"forge_cli.{name}\")\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\tdef _package_modules(package: str) -> list[ModuleType]:\n    77\t    \"\"\"The canonical ``forge_cli.<package>`` module plus, once it is a package, every\n    78\t    submodule of it (imported so their globals exist), root first.\"\"\"\n    79\t\n    80\t    root = package_module(package)\n    81\t    modules = [root]\n    82\t    for info in pkgutil.iter_modules(getattr(root, \"__path__\", [])):\n    83\t        modules.append(importlib.import_module(f\"forge_cli.{package}.{info.name}\"))\n    84\t    return modules\n    85\t\n    18\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\n    19\tTOOLS = ROOT / \"scripts/codex_orch_tools.py\"\n    20\tFIXTURES = ROOT / \"tests/fixtures\"\n    21\tPREFIX_WEDGE_FIXTURE = ROOT / \"tests/_fixtures/prefix-wedge-d77d997\"\n    22\tUNREPLAYABLE_CHAIN_ID = \"c-2026-08-21T223925Z-1490\"\n    23\tUNREPLAY